\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O King of kings, O Lord of Hosts,
\par Whose throne is lifted high
\par Above the nations of the earth, 
\par The armies of the sky,
\par The spirits of the perfected may
\par Give their thier nobler songs,
\par And we, Thy children, worship
\par Thee, to whom all praise belongs.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou who didst lead Thy people
\par Forth, and make the captive free,
\par Hast drawn arround our native
\par Land the curtain of the sea,
\par To make another holy place, where
\par Golden lamps should shine,
\par And human hearts keep loving
\par Watch arround the ark divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou who hast sown the sky with
\par Stars, setting Thy thoughts in gold,
\par Hast crowned our nation's life, and 
\par Ours, with blessings manifold;
\par Thy mercies have been numberless; 
\par Thy love, Thy grace, Thy care,
\par Were wider than our utmost need,
\par And higher than our prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O King of kings, O Lord of hosts,
\par Our fathers' God and ours!
\par Be with us in the future years;
\par And if the tempest lowers,
\par Look through the cloud with light
\par Of love, and smile our tears away,
\par And lead us through the brightening 
\par Years to heaven's eternal day.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

